# radiation_exposure_handling.md
**NOTE:** The scenarios described here are fictional lore and not part of the current engine.

Quantum hardware used by the engine may emit minor radiation when operating near peak capacity. The following guidelines summarize safe handling procedures.

## Precautions

- Operate all prototype hardware in a shielded rack with active cooling.
- Wear dosimeters when servicing the system or replacing components.
- Power down the cluster at the first sign of overheating or unexpected radiation alarms.
- Follow local regulations and facility rules for radiation safety training.

See [quantum_peril_scenarios.md](quantum_peril_scenarios.md) for failure states that can trigger exposure.
